ence because of the technology  it is what you do with the technology  it's what you do with a medium it's so  special I understand you know said this  and I think it's a perfect sentiment is  that 2d animation became the scapegoat  for bad storytelling well the audience  just don't want to watch his bad movies  right they like watching good movies the  thing I always tell students that really  wanted to work in animation or work in  film for that  is do not forget to study the basics  basic drawing even for computer  animation you should know how to draw  basic design the basic fundamentals of  animation where you learn the principles  of animation film grammar how do you  stage things you know that you know how  they do it in live-action filmmaking  story writing three active story  structure is so vital to this and if  you've got to learn all these basics  because this is kind of like eating  vegetables you know a lot of people  don't want to do it they just get on to  the more flashy stuff of using all the  latest software but the thing is is  through your career the software will  change it will always evolve and get  better what's important in remember this  software never makes a movie  entertaining is what you do with a  software and what you do with a software  it will be will be  you know you'll learn that from the  basic fundamentals you know I rely on  these the basic fundamentals of art and  design and filmmaking and animation and  storytelling you know every single day  of my career it's something that just is  a part of use the foundation in which  you work and without those you know you  won't go anywhere so it's really  important to get the fundamentals down  I loved animation I knew it was not just  for kids Walt Disney never made his  movies just for kids he made them for  everybody  Chuck Jones made his cartoons to show in  theaters in front of Warner Brothers  movies for adults but I felt it had to  be done for today's audience it had to  be done in a new way I found the answer  when I was working at Disney computer  animation I knew this was it I knew this  was the future you see one of the things  that that I  was admired about Walt Disney was his  innovative spirit Walt had been a great  advocate of the new and many  groundbreaking developments of film  technology had their origins at his  studio I threw myself into suggesting  projects that would show how the  computer could be used to take Disney  Disney animation to the next level I  even did a test I kept getting the  answers no that's not how it's done is  it cheaper is it faster then no just do  what you're told no one was willing to  take risks but that didn't stop me I  kept trying I just couldn't let go of  the idea that computer animation was  something Disney should be doing because  I knew it make this studio and its films  better then one day the manager of the  animation department mr. noh himself  called me into his office and fired me  to be fired from the place of your  dreams was so painful and embarrassing  for me that it took decades before I  could actually tell people about it  I made this kind of excuse up that I  followed my dream somewhere else  even as I got married I it took me you a  long time to tell Nancy Etta actually  get my wife I had actually gotten fired  but as fate would have it I met edy  camel of the Lucas home computer  division he and his group were doing the  most innovative research in the world in  computer graphics and unlike the Disney  that just fired me edy was so excited  about what I was trying to do to combine  classic animation principles to computer  animation I finally found someone who  could see the future as I saw it he  invited me to come work with him then in  1986 Steve Jobs entered our lives he was  so excited about what he what we were  trying to do  to Daddy that he bought our group from  Lucasfilm and we formed a new company  called Pixar he really pushed us to do  what no one else had ever done before  the result in 1995 we released the first  computer animated feature film ever made  we released Toy Story  [Applause]
 

